<<~ ahu #/head>>

! MemeProvider ~ one fan-out, three scales

Automerge replays every historical patch to a vessel that connects. Fanning those straight out
deserializes one URI eight or more times, hands TW5 hundreds of `addTiddler` calls before its first
refresh, and makes disk write-back hammer the filesystem for a state that has already moved on.

''MemeProvider stands between the handle and the projections'' so each projection meets settled state
rather than the replay.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! What this file binds

''The nalu shore stands at'' `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/projection-nalu#/enaction` — the
threshold, the per-bag union, the storm gate's progress guarantee and the scale fork read as the
PATTERN, shared with the disk, DOM and mempalace nalus. What follows names the invariants this file
owns on top of it.

# ''The caller owns the handle.'' MemeProvider imports no Automerge and reads only `path[0]` off a raw
patch, so the same implementation runs in Node and in a browser without a platform branch.
# ''The document reads at FIRE time, never at patch time.'' A debounce that captured state on arrival
would deliver a value the doc has already moved past; reading at the flush delivers the latest.
# ''Eligibility binds to the save cascade.'' A key enters the fan-out on `lar:` or `Draft of ` and on
nothing else — `$:/temp/` and `$:/` system tiddlers never enter the store, so fanning them out would
announce changes to records that do not exist. Whatever the adaptor writes, the provider carries.
# ''Sync-complete binds to an ISLAND, never to the provider.'' `markSyncComplete(islandId)` stays
idempotent per island; a single-doc vessel uses the default id, and each handle in a multi-bag vessel
calls with its own once ready.
# ''A late projection enters live, never buffering.'' Registering after an island completed fires
`onSyncComplete` for every already-complete island immediately — a projection built after the vessel
opened would otherwise wait for a signal that already passed.
# ''A projection that declares no changeset keeps its per-URI path.'' Opting out of the bulk path
costs a projection nothing but the count of its calls.
# ''A projection's throw stays its own.'' Every callback runs guarded, so one failing projection
reports and the fan-out continues to the rest.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-source>>

!! Where the bytes live

The implementation stands at `packages/lararium-mesh/src/meme-provider.ts`, and this carrier names its
law rather than holding its lines. ''A carrier that pastes a source file states nothing a reader could
not read at the source, and it goes stale in silence'' — the paste that stood here had drifted a third
of its substantial lines, still naming a boolean sync gate where the source carries a per-island set,
and omitting the changeset path entirely.

A live wiki transcludes the source into place at read time. Until it breathes, the pointer above IS
the reference, and the law below it stays the part a reader needs anyway.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

